1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Nf3 c5 6. dxc5 Qa5 7. Bd3 Qxc5 8. Qe2 { [%cal Gc1e3] } 8... O-O (8... Bg4 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Lines transpose. }) 9. Be3 Qa5 10. O-O Bg4 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Here, white has completed development and has the potential for a kingside push while black has a misplaced queen and is less complete in development. However, in this position, black's dark-squared bishop is much better. } { [%csl Gf3,Ge3,Gd3,Gc3,Gb8,Ga8][%cal Gg2g5,Gh2h5,Ga1d1,Gf1e1,Gf8d8,Gg7b2] } *


