1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. e5 dxe5 8. fxe5 Nd5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Nh5 is a more accurate move. } 9. Nxd5 Qxd5 10. c3 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Defending the d pawn from a bishop pin on the knight. } { [%cal Gc3d4,Gc8g4] } 10... Bg4 11. Qe2 Rad8 12. Be4 Qd7 13. h3 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] White wants the bishop out of there to start a kingside push. } 13... Be6 14. O-O { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Nice rook. } { [%csl Gf1] } 14... Bd5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black offers to exchange one of his key defenders and removes the blockade on the e pawn. } 15. Bxd5 Qxd5 16. Bf4 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Defending the crucial pawn. } 16... b5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black seeks an advance on the queenside, but nothing is happening over there. It's better to try to defend. } 17. Rad1 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] The e file for the rook here is better, especially with Bobby's plan to push. } 17... a6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Defending the pawn from any future captures. } 18. b3 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Supporting a potential c4 break to kick the queen from its strong central square. } 18... Na5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Here, black should play e6 to stop white from playing it. } 19. e6 Rc8 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Defending the c pawn. } (19... fxe6 20. Bxc7) 20. exf7+ Rxf7 21. Ng5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] A very strong square for the knight and kicking the rook. } 21... Rf6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] The only logical move. } 22. Rde1 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Bobby wastes a tempo from when he played Rad1. } 22... b4 23. Ne6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black is trying to play on the queenside but there's no time. Here, the engine recommends Rxe6 to stop the attack. } 23... bxc3 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] It's a big mistake to allow Nxg7. } 24. Nxg7 Qxd4+ { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] A pointless check. } 25. Kh2 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Here, black resigns. Black cannot capture the knight because of Qxe7+ followed by Be5. } 25... Kxg7 26. Qxe7+ Kg8 27. Be5 *


