1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. f4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. h3 Bxf3 7. Qxf3 O-O { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black should definitely wait to castle to hope to avoid white's attack. } 8. e5 dxe5 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] The engine likes Nc6, but most humans would take. } 9. dxe5 Nfd7 10. Qxb7 Nb6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black has to give up the b2 pawn and save his rook. } 11. Be3 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Attacking the knight. } 11... Qc8 12. Qxc8 Rxc8 13. O-O-O { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] White is up a pawn and is in a much less awkward position, with control of the d file, the bishop pair, and black still needs a couple more moves to finish development. } 13... c6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Blocking the knight's most natural development square. } 14. Be2 e6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black made two consecutive pawn moves when he should have been developing his pieces. None of black's pieces are doing anything important. } 15. Ne4 Nd5 16. Bd2 Nd7 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Finally developing his knights and grabbing the d5 square. } 17. c4 Ne7 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] The knight should have gone to b6. Here, black is just losing a knight. } 18. Bb4 c5 19. Rxd7 cxb4 20. Rxe7 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Easy play for white. } 20... Bf8 21. Rb7 Rcb8 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Don't trade. } 22. Rxb8 Rxb8 23. Rd1 Bh6 24. g3 a5 25. Rd7 Bg7 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] White's bishop should be on f8 to stop the advance of the pawn. } 26. c5 Kf8 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Black should block with the rook before bringing his king into the game to stop c6. } 27. c6 Rb6 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] The idea here is to get behind the passed pawn, but white has Rd8+, which is completely crushing. } 28. c7 { [%anno "hexachess", hexachess] Here, black resigned. There is nothing to do. } *


